-- AM (ART_PROVENANCE) -->
-- Drops the frame-grab provenance table added in 157 and extended in 158.
--
-- Recording where a cover was cut from only pays off with a background job to cut
-- it again, a progress screen, and a retry path for the frames that cannot be
-- reproduced - a lot of machinery for something most libraries never use. The
-- feature is withdrawn rather than left half-built.
--
-- Removed by a new migration rather than by rewriting 157 and deleting 158:
-- devices that already ran those are at schema version 158, and presenting them a
-- schema that stops at 157 makes SQLite take its downgrade path, which throws on
-- open. Applied migrations are history; this is the correction.
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS custom_art_source;
-- <-- AM (ART_PROVENANCE)
